Well, I found my bag back where I left it, on DL 7. The blessed amulet
turned out to be Reflection; unfortunately Sokoban zoo had another AoR
instead of BoH. Then I had a few lucky breaks: biggest general store I
ever seen (6x10?) on DL 11, throne room on DL 12 (not that I got
anything out of it except lots of pet food), Big Room with relatively
weak monsters (no giants or couatls) on DL 13, and a chaotic Temple on
DL 14. Finally I can sacrifice things!

After my dragon enjoyed a Shopkeeper Special, I used one SoC from the
store to charge up the uncursed marker (and apparently blessed it in
the process), immediately wrote another SoC and charged up the blessed
marker. Two or three absolutely necessary scrolls later, I now have
markers with 37 and 24 charges. What do you recommend I should save
them for? I now have Remove Curse spell, so need no SoRC, and do not
want to waste markers on Enchant weapons/armor. I do not yet know SoG,
and am reluctant to risk writing an unknown scroll. I considered
writing several SoMM in order to find vaults (and hopefully a portal to
Fort Ludios), but vaults can be found with PoOD, and nymphs are
plentiful. Basically, my question is - what kind of emergency
justifies using a marker which can no longer be recharged? Oh, and my
only wand of Cold is at (1:0); I'll probably need to recharge it
again to deal with water levels.

